{"title":"2009 Zhautykov International Olympiad Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all pairs of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />, such that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/34504ec6abb78e0f5a2a37464f0303dd348db61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 2009y + 2y^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"167\" height=\"18\" />.</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 Zhautykov International Olympiad Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, such that there exist a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/322dbdcd983a78f64982e6d5d37b926a54c92a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f: \\mathbb{R}\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> satisfying the following inequality:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/1/6917ef956b9cfc0828cfc34250b25b397afcaf72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + af(y)\\leq y + f(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" /></center>\n<p>for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b5c9755a11dfd9dea1da1dcd236e268bad8675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 Zhautykov International Olympiad Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For a convex hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> with an area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, prove that:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d34e299c8bf6393bbc5553f97c9a44c6ee23bcb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC\\cdot(BD + BF - DF) + CE\\cdot(BD + DF - BF) + AE\\cdot(BF + DF - BD)\\geq 2\\sqrt {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"669\" height=\"21\" />.</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 Zhautykov International Olympiad Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>On the plane, a Cartesian coordinate system is chosen. Given points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f58b9ad1b88b97348253eb4386ec6e0612d542.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,A_2,A_3,A_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> on the parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca7ebfe4cb06e20c204fa1dc02267597aad658cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />, and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/46498ff7a82b417cd22da627a7b5d61789d16a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1,B_2,B_3,B_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" /> on the parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498e0f214a152688e90ccebb75272829e05e0068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2009x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f58b9ad1b88b97348253eb4386ec6e0612d542.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,A_2,A_3,A_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> are concyclic, and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2744600189f7f1df31756f2022b2d5212ef1c767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f7ff1d2561a1aeb9c1e6a0e4a4cc2da1bab71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> have equal abscissas for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7aa0b885ce0b7603f4d83fdb853d120a1085397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1,2,3,4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />.\nProve that points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/46498ff7a82b417cd22da627a7b5d61789d16a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1,B_2,B_3,B_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" /> are also concyclic.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 Zhautykov International Olympiad Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given a quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5ffca17e8f5d2f04ce60175add21df4eef9a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\angle D = 90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"128\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> so taht <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41a3fd7eec331c415a931b404fd0a137c618a364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = AM$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />. Rays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5d96c8d1e481244e028c9e97d1d7b53206536b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> intersect at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> are feet of perpendiculars from points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. \nProve that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e603e626fb081605724e889fe3fc078956ecb16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MHN = \\angle MCK$\" width=\"153\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 Zhautykov International Olympiad Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a checked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f4c96ceee0994d0c1f425d8133ce7df11f1b72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17\\times 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> table, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> squares are colored in black. We call a line any of rows, columns, or any of two diagonals of the table. In one step, if at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the squares in some line are black, then one can paint all the squares of this line in black. Find the minimal value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that for some initial arrangement of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> black squares one can paint all squares of the table in black in some steps.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Zhautykov_International_Olympiad_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 Zhautykov International Olympiad Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017231621\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 208/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6658/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7730:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017231621 and revision id 29916. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}